{
  "name": "Basic Formal Ontology Building Blocks",
  "abstract": "Building blocks for Basic Formal Ontology (BFO) - ISO/IEC 21838-2:2020 compliant top-level \nontology providing classes and relations common to all areas of scientific investigation.\n",
  "description": "This repository contains building blocks for **Basic Formal Ontology (BFO)** 2020, a top-level \nontology conformant to the requirements specified in ISO/IEC 21838-1 for top-level ontologies.\n\nBFO contains classes and relations representing content common to all areas of scientific \ninvestigation, such as:\n\n- **Entity**: The root class of all things\n- **Continuant**: Entities that persist through time (objects, qualities, sites)\n- **Occurrent**: Entities that occur or happen in time (processes, temporal regions)\n- **Material Entity**: Physical entities like organisms, artifacts\n- **Process**: Occurrent entities that unfold through time\n- **Quality**: Dependent continuants that are qualities\n- **Role**: Realizable entities that are roles\n\nBFO is used as a top-level architecture by numerous ontologies in:\n\n- The Open Biomedical and Biomedical Ontologies (OBO) Foundry\n- The Industrial Ontologies Foundry (IOF)\n- The Common Core Ontologies (CCO) suite\n\nOntologies conformant to BFO promote interoperability, standardization, and reuse among \ndomain-level ontologies.\n",
